    "question": "What regularizers were used to encourage consistency in back translation cycles?",
    "answer": "Cycle consistency loss regularizers were used, specifically `cycle(F, G, X) = 1/n ∑_i ∆(xi, G(F(xi)))` and `cycle(F, G, Y) = 1/m ∑_j ∆(yj, F(G(yj)))`, where ∆ is the average cosine similarity.",
    "evidence": "We introduce `cycle(F, G, X) = 1/n ∑_i=1^n ∆(xi, G(F(xi))), `cycle(F, G, Y) = 1/m ∑_j=1^m ∆(yj , F(G(yj ))), (2) where ∆ denotes the discrepancy criterion, which is set as the average cosine similarity in our model."
  },
  {
    "question": "What are new best results on standard benchmark?",
    "answer": "The proposed method obtains the best published results on the Vecmap benchmark, with Ours-GeoMMsemi achieving state-of-the-art results on all tested language pairs except EN-FI, and being fully unsupervised.",
